; GRIFO - sprite tiles, 8x16 sprite mode (LCDC bit 2 = 1). Drawn by pixel-artist.
; HARD RULE: every 8x16 piece = 2 consecutive tiles, top at an EVEN index, bottom at the next.
; 16x16 object at label NAME (4 tiles): NAME+0 left-top, NAME+1 left-bottom,
;                                      NAME+2 right-top, NAME+3 right-bottom
;   => sprite A (x, y) tile NAME, sprite B (x+8, y) tile NAME+2.
; 8x8 objects (bullets, side shot) = top tile + BLANK bottom tile (no two objects share a pair).
; Shade 0 ('.') is transparent. Drawn for OBP0 = 0xE4. Hit flash (OBP1) e.g. 0x90 or 0x40.
;
; Flips: everything faces its travel direction (player up, enemies down); all are symmetric
; or stored in both versions, EXCEPT SHOT_SIDE: drawn for the RIGHT side shot (up-right,
; vx > 0); the left side shot = SHOT_SIDE with S_FLIPX.
; PLAYER_BANK_R is PLAYER_BANK_L mirrored (stored, so no flip code is needed; to save 4 tiles
;   use BANK_L with S_FLIPX and swap the two 8-px columns, then delete BANK_R).
; Animations: DART/WAVE/SWOOP/CARRIER _0/_1 every 8 f. EXPLO_0 (small) 8 f -> EXPLO_1 (large) 8 f.
;   PEXPLO_0/1/2 (player death) ~11 f each (32 f). ITEM_P/ITEM_B blink OBP0/OBP1 every 8 f.
; Player shots: SHOT1 (level 1, 4x12 beam), SHOT2 (level 2-3 double beam, 8x12), both in a
;   pair (12 rows used); hitbox center (X+4, Y+8) matches the art. SHOT_SIDE 4x8-ish.
; EBULLET 6x6 round (pixels 1..6), EBULLET_BOSS 6x6 diamond: center at (X+4, Y+4) of the top tile.

@ PLAYER
; 0
.......#
......#+
.....#-+
....#-#-
##..#---
#+#..#-#
#++###+-
#+++-#+#

